"comparison": "Both AMD and Broadcom disclose risks arising from the inaccuracy of customer demand estimates used to make production and supply chain decisions, which can lead to mismatches between supply and demand. AMD explicitly links these estimation failures to the risk of excess or obsolete inventory and subsequent write-downs that adversely affect gross margins. Broadcom similarly warns that decisions based on potentially inaccurate customer estimates could lead to an inability to maintain appropriate manufacturing capacity and yields, or result in overestimation of demand leading to excess capacity.",
