"comparison": "AMD and NVIDIA both identify the failure to estimate customer demand accurately as a direct cause of mismatches between supply and demand, leading to adverse financial outcomes. While AMD focuses on the risk of excess or obsolete inventory resulting from such mismatches and its impact on gross margins, NVIDIA explicitly states that these mismatches have resulted in both product shortages and excess inventory, and have 'significantly harmed' financial results. Both disclosures underscore the material consequence of inaccurate forecasting on inventory management and profitability.",
