"comparison": "Both AMD and Qualcomm describe risks associated with ordering manufacturing and supply based on demand forecasts that may be inaccurate or not fully covered by binding customer commitments, leading to potential excess or obsolete inventory. AMD warns that cancellation or deferral of orders can result in excess inventory and write-downs affecting gross margins. Qualcomm similarly notes that if demand is overestimated and not covered by binding commitments, it may experience increased excess or obsolete inventory or reserve charges, negatively impacting results of operations.",
